course: dictionary
lesson: 14750
title: Propagate: many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Mum took cuttings from the spider plant to propagate it.» Cuttings and plant are the clues, so propagate means to grow new plants from a parent plant.
explain: «The rumour began to propagate around the school within an hour.» Here propagate means to spread, so many people hear the news. Ask yourself: what is moving or spreading? The rumour is spreading.
explain: «Sound can propagate through water and solids, but not through space.» In science, propagate means for sound, light or waves to travel through something. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Propagate is a verb, so it shows an action: propagate, propagates, propagated, propagating.
fact: «Propagate» can mean to grow new plants from cuttings, seeds or runners.
fact: «Propagate» can also mean to spread an idea, news or belief to many people.
fact: In science, «propagate» means that sound, light or waves travel through something.
fact: «Propagate» shares its root with «propaganda», which is information spread to persuade people.
exercise: «Mum took cuttings to propagate the spider plant.» What does propagate mean here? | To water a plant every day | To stop a plant from growing | To paint a plant green | *To grow new plants from a parent plant
exercise: «The rumour began to propagate around the school.» What does propagate mean here? | To go to sleep | To disappear quietly | To fall to the ground | *To spread to many people
exercise: «Sound can propagate through water.» What does propagate mean in this sentence? | To paint a picture of water | To grow new plants from seeds | To freeze solid in cold weather | *To travel through something, as sound does
test: «The frogs propagate in the spring pond.» What does propagate mean? | *To breed or reproduce | To sing loudly | To swim away | To freeze solid
test: Which sentence uses propagate to mean spread an idea? | *«The leaders wanted to propagate their belief to everyone in the town.» | «We propagated the seeds in the garden shed.» | «The dog will propagate its tail when it sleeps.» | «The sun began to propagate slowly over the hill.»
exam: Jayden reads «propagate» in a science text about waves. Which meaning fits best? | To breed a new kind of fish | To grow new plants from cuttings | *For waves to travel through something | To spread quickly across a room
